      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood’s eponymous park was officially acquired in 1920, becoming a green heart for residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.rcpna.org/history-of-rose-city-park/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Other historic parks in the area include Normandale (1940), Frazer (1950, once a juvenile detention center), and the western part of Rose City Golf Course (1920).",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.rcpna.org/history-of-rose-city-park/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1946 Nabisco proposed a 24‑acre factory in the neighborhood, but the plan was dropped by June 1947 for a site in Piedmont.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.rcpna.org/history-of-rose-city-park/",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A statue of George Washington, sculpted by Pompeo Coppini, was dedicated on July 4, 1927, and once stood at 57th and Sandy.",
